menu "Dhara FTL Configuration"

    config DHARA_MAP_PATH_CACHE
        bool "Enable sequential-locality path cache in dhara_map"
        default y
        help
            Caches the last successful read-only dhara_map_find() path
            traversal. Consecutive sector lookups that share a common
            radix-tree prefix with the previous lookup skip the
            already-known levels, reducing dhara_journal_read_meta() calls
            for sequential sector access patterns.

            This grows in-RAM struct dhara_map by 140 bytes. Disable this to
            recover that RAM at the cost of losing the read-path speedup.

endmenu
